---
import { site } from "../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const operatorName = site.legalName ?? "CareMin";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | CareMin"
  description="How CareMin collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>How CareMin collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 11 August 2026</p>

      <aside class="legal-summary" aria-labelledby="privacy-summary-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-summary-title">Our privacy commitments</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Customer operational data stored by the CareMin application is hosted in Australia.
          </li>
          <li>We do not sell personal information or share it for advertising.</li>
          <li>
            Customer operational data is not shared with other CareMin customers, data brokers, or
            unrelated third parties.
          </li>
          <li>
            Information is used only to provide, secure, support, and administer CareMin, follow
            customer instructions, or meet legal obligations.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <h2>About this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains how {operatorName} (referred to as <q>CareMin</q>, <q>we</q>, <q>us</q
        >, or <q>our</q>) handles personal information through the public CareMin website, the
        CareMin application, product demonstrations, support, and related business activities. We
        handle personal information in accordance with applicable Australian privacy law, including
        the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles where they apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        A customer agreement may contain additional privacy, confidentiality, retention, and data
        handling commitments. If a customer agreement provides stronger protections, those
        protections continue to apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>

      <h3>Website enquiries and business contact information</h3>
      <p>
        When you arrange a walkthrough or contact us, we may collect your name, work email address,
        organisation, number of homes, message, consent to be contacted, and subsequent
        correspondence. The public form is intended for business contact information only. Do not
        submit resident information, health information, payroll records, or other sensitive
        operational data through the website form.
      </p>

      <h3>Account and user information</h3>
      <p>
        When an organisation uses CareMin, we may collect authorised users' names, work contact
        details, organisation and facility associations, account roles, authentication records,
        preferences, and support communications.
      </p>

      <h3>Customer operational data</h3>
      <p>
        Customers may provide facility, workforce, roster, worked-hours, role-classification,
        occupied bed-day, reporting, source-file, evidence, and calculation information. This data
        may contain personal information about staff, contractors, residents, or other individuals.
        The customer controls what is submitted and is responsible for ensuring it has authority to
        collect and provide that information to CareMin.
      </p>

      <h3>Technical and security information</h3>
      <p>
        We and our infrastructure providers may process IP addresses, browser and device
        information, request timestamps, authentication events, system logs, error records, and
        security events. We use this information to deliver the service, diagnose faults, prevent
        misuse, and protect accounts and data.
      </p>

      <h2>How information is collected</h2>
      <p>We collect information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>directly from individuals through forms, accounts, demonstrations, and support;</li>
        <li>from a customer's authorised administrators and uploaded source systems;</li>
        <li>automatically when the website or application is accessed; and</li>
        <li>from service providers where necessary to operate, secure, or support CareMin.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use information only where reasonably necessary to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>respond to enquiries and arrange product walkthroughs;</li>
        <li>create and administer authorised accounts;</li>
        <li>provide CareMin's import, monitoring, calculation, evidence, and export functions;</li>
        <li>follow customer instructions and provide support;</li>
        <li>secure the service, investigate errors, and prevent unauthorised use;</li>
        <li>maintain business, billing, contractual, and audit records;</li>
        <li>
          improve reliability and usability using aggregated or de-identified information; and
        </li>
        <li>comply with legal obligations and resolve disputes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use customer operational data for advertising, data brokerage, or the benefit of
        other CareMin customers.
      </p>

      <h2>When information is disclosed</h2>
      <p>
        CareMin does not sell or rent personal information. We do not disclose customer operational
        data to advertisers, data brokers, other customers, or unrelated third parties. Information
        may be disclosed only in the following limited circumstances:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          to authorised users and administrators of the same customer organisation, according to
          their access permissions;
        </li>
        <li>
          to contracted providers that supply hosting, infrastructure, email or form delivery,
          security, monitoring, support, or professional services necessary to operate CareMin;
        </li>
        <li>when a customer instructs or authorises us to disclose it;</li>
        <li>
          to professional advisers who are subject to confidentiality obligations, where reasonably
          necessary;
        </li>
        <li>
          where required or authorised by law, a court or tribunal order, or a lawful government
          request; or
        </li>
        <li>
          as part of a proposed business transfer, subject to confidentiality and applicable law.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Service providers may process information only for the contracted service or another lawful
        purpose. Using a hosting, email, or infrastructure provider does not permit that provider to
        use customer operational data for its own advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Australian hosting and overseas processing</h2>
      <p>
        Customer operational data stored by the CareMin application is hosted in Australia. We
        select and configure the application's primary production data stores to keep this data in
        Australia.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some limited processing connected with the public website and business administration may
        occur outside Australia. The marketing website is delivered using Vercel's global network.
        Walkthrough enquiries are relayed through FormSubmit and an email provider, and may be
        processed in the United States or other countries in which those providers operate.
        FormSubmit states that form submissions may be retained in its archive for up to 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps when selecting and managing providers and limit the information
        sent to them to what is necessary for their service. Provider locations and infrastructure
        may change, and we will update this policy when a material change affects how personal
        information is handled.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use advertising cookies or cross-site behavioural tracking. Analytics are disabled
        by default on the public website. If analytics are enabled, CareMin will use a
        privacy-focused configuration and update this policy before collecting additional
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect information from misuse,
        interference, loss, and unauthorised access, modification, or disclosure. Measures may
        include access controls, authentication, logging, backups, secure network connections,
        provider due diligence, and limiting access to people who need it for their work.
      </p>
      <p>
        No internet or storage system is completely secure. Customers must protect their login
        details, assign access appropriately, and notify us promptly of suspected unauthorised use.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal information only for as long as it is reasonably needed for the purpose
        for which it was collected, to provide the service, meet contractual retention settings,
        resolve disputes, maintain legitimate business records, or comply with law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Customer operational data is retained and deleted in accordance with the applicable customer
        agreement and authorised customer instructions. Website enquiries may remain in business
        email records while the enquiry or commercial relationship is active. When information is no
        longer required, we take reasonable steps to delete it, de-identify it, or place it beyond
        use, subject to backup cycles and legal retention obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Access and correction</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask to access or correct personal information we hold about you. CareMin users may
        be able to update some account information directly or through their organisation's
        administrator. For other requests, contact us using the process below. We may need to verify
        your identity and may refuse a request where permitted by law, in which case we will explain
        the reason where required.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe CareMin has mishandled personal information, contact us and write
        <q>Privacy complaint</q> in the message. Please describe the issue and the outcome you are seeking.
        We will acknowledge the complaint, investigate it, and aim to respond within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the
        <a
          href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        The website links to government guidance, LinkedIn, and other external sites. Their privacy
        practices are governed by their own policies, not this policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy when our services, providers, or legal obligations change. The
        current version will be published on this page with its updated date. We will provide
        additional notice where a material change requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Direct privacy questions, access or correction requests, and complaints to the CareMin
        Privacy Officer through the <a href="/#contact">CareMin contact form</a>. Write
        <q>Privacy request</q> in the message so it can be directed appropriately.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Operator:</strong>
        {operatorName}{site.abn ? ` · ABN ${site.abn}` : ""}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
